{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553460-true-faith-vs-elder-vampire","id":1553460,"title":"True Faith vs Elder Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-26T10:00:41-07:00","id":1553460,"title":"True Faith vs Elder Vampire","content":"I have a player going all into a True Faith build and is preparing to square off against what he knows is an elder vampire. Im trying to articulate that isnt going to go as planned once you try to roll initiative.<br /> <br /> Conversely I have a second player interacting with some S.A.D. inquisition agents which I presume most likely he will want to defeat as well. <br /> <br /> Once they throw up those holy symbols, (or even before if the vampire knows that trick), there isnt much stopping them from using celerity and potence to use them as target practice with makeshift weapons.<br /> <br /> Any factors i should consider? What experiences have yall done with this type of scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T11:26:27-07:00","id":1553466,"title":"","content":"Always state the edition you're using to begin with. I'm guessing 5th, but that isn't a given around here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T11:53:58-07:00","id":1553469,"title":"","content":"We are using V20, but the concept is not dependant as all the splats add or take away from the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T14:30:00-07:00","id":1553470,"title":"","content":"It does sound like there is a gap in expectation setting while the game was being set up. If one player is expecting to take on an Elder Vampire with True Faith alone, and another player might be hoping to take on SAD agents... it seems the players have an expectation of either protagonist plot armor or PC effectiveness that isn't inherently warranted by a full understanding of the setting.<br /> <br /> As for editions... how dangerous SAD is, is very different if you're using the WoD5 version of them (where they're part of the Second Inquisition and get access to all sorts of high tech gadgets) vs. the earlier takes on them when they're just FBI agents that are usually in over their heads due to a lack of open support from the agency (and most of them aren't HRT squad members with high level combat training).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T15:29:07-07:00","id":1553472,"title":"","content":"So... few questions.<br /> <br /> 1. What level of true faith do they possess?<br /> 2. What is your stance on true faith above five dots like some in the Society of Leopold possess?<br /> 3. Are you using ONLY v-20 or are you also including the other supplements from over game lines? If I recall Mage had some rather interesting ideas for true faith that could make it stronger. They had true faith points which were equivalent to their true faith rating that were regained on rest. These points could be used for miracles a select few spell-like abilities of great use.<br /> <br /> <br /> You say a lot about initiative and the like but even at true faith one a mortal can keep a vampire at bay from a single successful roll either forcing them to retreat or freezing them in space on a failure, the only time this does not work is a botch. This is not a combat roll there is nothing preventing someone with true faith from keeping the cross or prayer running for every action in a scene. Difficulty being faith versus vampire's current willpower points. If they know they are approaching the vampire there is nothing stopping them from praying all the way, simply hearing the prayer or seeing the symbol brandished is what forces the check on the vampire it cost no resources and only triggers a roll when the vampire is in ear shot or sees the symbol if I read it correctly...<br /> <br /> Entry for true faith one.<br /> &quot;Any character with Faith may attempt toward off vampires by brandishing a holy symbol or uttering prayers. The person rolls Faith<br /> against a difficulty equal to the vampire\u2019s current Willpower points. The number of successes indicates the number of steps backward<br /> the vampire is forced to take. If no successes are scored, the vampire need not step back<br /> but may not advance. A botch indicates that the vampire may advance unhindered. Further, if the cross, Bible, or other holy symbol<br /> is placed against the vampire\u2019s body, each success causes an aggravated health level of<br /> damage, burning into the flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing is said about the roll being limited to combat only for the first effect.<br /> <br /> Even if the vampire knows the trick there is nothing stating that they can resist it. This aspect still works on everything but a botch, knowing it will come does nothing, as true faith once the roll succeeds cannot really be resisted the fifth dot may be resisted with constant willpower expenditure or a difficult roll.<br /> <br /> True faith five entry.<br /> <br /> &quot; The person is so pure, so holy, that they can fill a vampire with self-loathing, disgust, terror, and even physical pain. Any vampire hearing the person pray, preach, or recite psalms, or who is touched by the faithful, may be forced to flee immediately. A vampire who is unable to flee is reduced to a gibbering wreck, flailing on the floor and screaming, sobbing, or begging forgiveness. To avoid fleeing, the vampire must either expend one Willpower point per turn or make a Stamina roll each turn (difficulty of 5 + their own Intelligence) \u2013 the higher the vampire's Intelligence, the higher the difficulty, as the more tortured and guilty they feel.&quot;<br /> .<br /> Note pushing a vampire back with true faith one does not prevent them from attacking if they possess ranged weapons or disciplines. It does however prevent them from rushing you.<br /> <br /> True faith two provides resistance to mental disciplines with willpower expenditure for a few turns while true faith four grants complete immunity, and immunity to ghouling.<br /> <br /> I had a question for the others on this thread as well.<br /> <br /> The combat action does require a hit roll correct? As you must touch the vampire with the object or at least that is how I would read it...<br /> <br /> With the damage being the true faith successes on the willpower roll I assume this is actually sort of unclear. Or does the person with true faith during their turn just have the option to touch the vampire with their symbol and then do the true faith roll?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T17:44:34-07:00","id":1553474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553460-true-faith-vs-elder-vampire#post1553460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any factors i should consider? What experiences have yall done with this type of scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if players understand how you rule True Faith. True Faith has a lot of subjectivity to it, even if V20 improved this a bit, so it depends a lot on you.<br /> <br /> That said: TF isn't usually very good at being offensive, so while a user may greatly enhance a group, by themselves it isn't going to do much but let them flee. Elders are usually well protected too, so attacking one of them usually entails fighting a lot of servants and problems of all kinds. True Faith alone isn't a lot of help, not because it doesn't work against the Elder, but because engaging the Elder in melee is the last of your concerns.<br /> <br /> As a rule of thumb, engaging in direct confrontation is a losing strategy for everyone, any NPC worth their salt will stack things in their favor as much as possible and beyond. Elders so they never face true danger, hunters so they have an actual fighting chance. So TF may help things around, but won't be the winning factor by itself. If an actual direct confrontation ends up happening, though, the game is pretty much designed to give victory in a silver plate to the stronger supernatural after a fast and easy combat, that's not a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553460-true-faith-vs-elder-vampire?p=1553472#post1553472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a question for the others on this thread as well.<br /> <br /> The combat action does require a hit roll correct? As you must touch the vampire with the object or at least that is how I would read it...<br /> <br /> With the damage being the true faith successes on the willpower roll I assume this is actually sort of unclear. Or does the person with true faith during their turn just have the option to touch the vampire with their symbol and then do the true faith roll?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the target isn't offering any resistance, then yes, an attack roll is warranted, although it should not add to the damage rating. And this isn't necessarily an easy attack, it's up to the ST how much actual skin contact must happen, or how intense, so how hard is this attack is anyone's guess. Based solely on this description and the overall trope, I'd say this isn't meant to be actually a combat action, although there's no inherent problem in letting it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T05:13:42-07:00","id":1553477,"title":"","content":"The true faith player understands i have no qualm killing a PC. One died already in the game.<br /> <br /> Ive incorporated the mage rules of 3xp per pip. So while he is at TF lvl 4 he could later buy level 5 but never plans to hurt anyone. He is keeping a max humanity passive style. We agreed that TF should have all the best options available so incorporates the mage rules for TF bonuses and such. At 21 xp per pip it is more costly then disciplines. I doubt our campaign will be long enough for him to hit lvl 6+ but he seems psyched for it so we shall see.<br /> <br /> I remember one game we played and a TF locked down the group until someone grabbed silverware from a dinner table and yeeted it till the hunter died.<br /> <br /> Idk how he intends to passively handle the scenario but if he pulls his ace from his sleeve he will earn a lot of aggro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T06:08:24-07:00","id":1553479,"title":"","content":"Then you shouldn't worry much, no. Your players know what to expect and have their own plans, just let them go ahead.<br /> <br /> Players have an uncanny ability to defy expectations. No amount of experience will prepare you for that, roll with the flow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}